  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="b15f-4db1-2f76-5d6b" name="Picts (Age of Arthur) - List Notes" publicationId="28aa-c13e-b61d-4f3e" hidden="false">
      <description>THE PICTS (The Age of Arthur, pp.59-69). Units of Nobles and Warriors may have a Leader (+5), Musician (+5) and Standard (+5). Allies are documented only. Hunting Crossbow: range 24", Strength 3, no armour save modifier; may not move and shoot in the same turn.

ARMY COMPOSITIONS (pick one in the Army composition list):
[Picts - Early Southern Pictish Kingdoms]
  Characters: up to 33%
  Common Warriors: at least 33%
  Uncommon Warriors: up to 25%
  THE EARLY SOUTHERN PICTISH KINGDOMS. Characters up to 33% (led by a Chieftain, or a Mormaer upgraded to Army General; no Christian Priest). Common warriors at least 33% (Nobles and Warriors). Uncommon up to 25% (Hunters and Hunting Dogs). Allies up to 25% from one list: Romano-British Civitates - Twilight of Britannia (Milites and Pedyt), Scots-Irish (Scotti Raiders and Settlers) or Saxons (Sea Raiders). Mounted Nobles may exchange ponies for horses (+3).
[Picts - Later Southern Pictish Kingdoms]
  Characters: up to 33%
  Common Warriors: at least 33%
  Uncommon Warriors: up to 25%
  THE LATER SOUTHERN PICTISH KINGDOMS. Characters up to 33% (led by a Chieftain, or a Mormaer upgraded to Army General; either a Magus or a Christian Priest, not both). Common warriors at least 33% (Nobles and Warriors). Uncommon up to 25% (Hunters and Hunting Dogs). Allies up to 25% from one list: British and Welsh Kingdoms - the Welsh Kingdoms in the North, Scots-Irish (Dalriada) or Saxons (Anglian Kingdoms of the Heptarchy). Nobles and Warriors may exchange ponies for horses (+3). Optional Pictish thrusting spears (documented): Nobles and Warriors on foot become ordinary heavy infantry (up to +3 rank bonus, but only +2 for Leadership); Nobles exchange throwing spears and bucklers for thrusting spears and shields (free); Warriors exchange mixed weapons and bucklers for thrusting spears, javelins and shields (+1).
[Picts - Picts of the North]
  Characters: up to 33%
  Common Warriors: at least 33%
  Uncommon Warriors: up to 25%
  THE PICTS OF THE NORTH. Characters up to 33% (no Chieftain: led by a Mormaer upgraded to Army General; no Christian Priest). Common warriors at least 33% (Nobles and Warriors). Uncommon up to 25% (Hunters and Hunting Dogs). Allies up to 25% from the Scots-Irish (Dalriada). Nobles may not have light armour or horses.
[Picts - The Attecotti]
  Characters: up to 40%
  Common Warriors: at least 33%
  Uncommon Warriors: up to 25%
  THE ATTECOTTI. Characters up to 40% (no Chieftain: led by a Mormaer upgraded to Army General). Common warriors at least 33% (Nobles and Warriors). Uncommon up to 25% (Hunters and Hunting Dogs). Allies up to 25% from the Scots-Irish (Dalriada). All Nobles and Warriors are Fierce (even if mounted; documented only). Nobles may not have light armour or horses.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
